{
  "id": "rabbitmq-mitm",
  "title": "RabbitMQ broker under MITM attacks (reduced CSG)",
  "chapter": "Use case 6 — RabbitMQ broker under attack",
  "chapterOrder": 6,
  "formalism": "csg",
  "tool": "PRISM-games 3.x",
  "summary": "An attacker (CAPEC-384, man in the middle) and the sensors play concurrently at the RabbitMQ southbound bridge. The attacker tampers with the payload or with the routing key; the attack frequency depends on the attack type (DoS, ARP spoofing, Mirai).",
  "description": [
    "Each round the sensors choose to send a message or stay idle, and the attacker chooses to tamper with the payload, tamper with the routing key, or wait. The non-player RabbitMQ_Broker module records the outcome in buf: 1 = delivered, 2 = payload tampered, 3 = message unrouted (wrong routing key, the target queue stays empty).",
    "An attack succeeds with probability p_att = 1 − e^(−t_round / (MTBA · BAN)), where MTBA is the mean time between attacks of the chosen scenario (1 = DoS, 2 = ARP spoofing, 3 = Mirai). In the reference study, the MTBA is extracted from a Canadian Institute for Cybersecurity dataset.",
    "Mitigation: banning the attacker (as recommended by RabbitMQ) lengthens the time between attacks. Set BAN > 1 to model it.",
    "Reduced teaching model: the MTBA values are illustrative, chosen to reproduce the trend of the full study (ARP > Mirai > DoS, payload tampering close to 1 after 30 rounds). Exact figures require the full broker model."
  ],
  "objectives": [
    "Turn an attack frequency measured on data into a per-round success probability.",
    "Express tampering and message loss as rPATL properties with coalitions.",
    "Assess a countermeasure by changing one parameter."
  ],
  "exercises": [
    "Compare <<att>> and <<att,sen>> for the tampering property. Why is the attacker alone at 0?",
    "Run the tampering property for SCENARIO = 1, 2, 3 and k = 1…30 (Experiment in PRISM). Which attack is the most harmful?",
    "Set BAN = 10: how much does the expected number of unrouted messages drop over 30 rounds?"
  ],
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "k",
      "label": "Number of rounds",
      "value": "30",
      "description": "Horizon of the bounded properties"
    },
    {
      "name": "SCENARIO",
      "label": "Attack scenario",
      "value": "2",
      "description": "1 = DoS, 2 = ARP spoofing, 3 = Mirai"
    },
    {
      "name": "BAN",
      "label": "Ban factor (mitigation)",
      "value": "1",
      "description": "1 = no mitigation; 10 = time between attacks ten times longer"
    },
    {
      "name": "t_round",
      "label": "Round duration",
      "value": "1",
      "unit": "time unit"
    }
  ],
